@startuml
title Mark price — a median over three independent estimates
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam PackageBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ComponentFontColor #1F3A5F
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1F3A5F
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #4A78B5

package "Candidate 1 — external spot, corrected for basis" {
  [Oracle price] as C1A
  [+ 150 s EMA of\n(Hyperliquid mid - oracle)] as C1B
  C1A -right-> C1B
}

package "Candidate 2 — Hyperliquid's own book" {
  [Median of best bid,\nbest ask, last trade] as C2
}

package "Candidate 3 — external perp market" {
  [Weighted median of Binance 3,\nOKX 2, Bybit 2, Gate.io 1, MEXC 1\nperpetual mid prices] as C3
}

[Median of the candidates] as MED
C1B --> MED
C2 --> MED
C3 --> MED

[Mark price] as MARK
MED --> MARK

note right of MED
  If exactly two of the three exist,
  a 30 s EMA of candidate 2 joins as
  a fourth input, so the median is
  never taken over a single source.
end note

note bottom of MARK
  Drives margin, liquidation, TP/SL triggering
  and unrealised PnL. Recomputed whenever
  validators publish, so roughly every 3 s.
  Funding does not use it.
end note
@enduml
